        "original_id": "fe443d86-923a-5a8f-bff6-9e611b0fd927",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Phacelia, Nymphaea\n- Animals: Eucosma hennei\n- Places: North America, South America, El Segundo sand dunes, California\n- Habitats: open sand, undisturbed sand dunes, dense shrubs\n- Concepts: genera, species, herbaceous plants, aquatic plants, larval host plants\n\nFacts:\n- Phacelia is a genus of about 200 species of annual or perennial herbaceous plants native to North and South America.\n- Nymphaea is a genus of hardy and tender aquatic plants in the family Nymphaeaceae.\n- Eucosma hennei specimens have been recovered in the El Segundo sand dunes in California.\n- The habitat of Eucosma hennei includes open sand, undisturbed sand dunes, and dense shrubs populated with the larval host plant Phacelia.",
